  "excerpt": "Baccala alla Vicentina is a long-braised dish from Vicenza in the Veneto, where salt cod is slowly cooked in milk with onions, anchovies, parmesan, and olive oil until it becomes almost creamy and spreadable. Despite the name, the dish uses stockfish rather than salted cod. Serves 4 to 6.",
